1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,649
A funnel narrows a whole market down to a short list, by itself.

2
00:00:03,699 --> 00:00:06,828
It starts from a pool, such as the top five hundred coins,

3
00:00:06,848 --> 00:00:10,677
and checks them in stages, from the daily chart down to the hour.

4
00:00:11,133 --> 00:00:13,460
Funnels live in Angstrom Lattice.

5
00:00:13,510 --> 00:00:18,204
Angstrom provides four to start from: crypto and equities, longs and shorts.

6
00:01:13,903 --> 00:01:17,894
Each stage checks one Set, at each close of its own timeframe.

7
00:01:17,944 --> 00:01:22,062
Only the assets that hold every stage before it are checked at the next one.

8
00:01:22,505 --> 00:01:24,938
A provided funnel can't be changed.

9
00:01:24,988 --> 00:01:29,214
Press Make my own copy, and your copy runs for your account, every hour.

10
00:01:29,657 --> 00:01:31,300
In your copy, choose the pool:

11
00:01:31,320 --> 00:01:35,056
the top fifty, a minimum daily volume, or just your watchlist.

12
00:01:35,106 --> 00:01:39,000
By default an asset leaves a stage only after two No answers in a row,

13
00:01:39,020 --> 00:01:41,166
so it doesn't flicker in and out.

14
00:01:41,601 --> 00:01:45,080
Under Stages, your Sets sit on the left, as in Prism Scan.

15
00:01:45,130 --> 00:01:47,971
Drag one onto a stage, or press plus to add a stage,

16
00:01:47,991 --> 00:01:50,272
and pick when each stage is checked.

17
00:01:50,735 --> 00:01:54,832
Flagged means every stage holds but the last: it's on the shortlist.

18
00:01:54,882 --> 00:01:57,380
Candidate means every stage holds.

19
00:01:57,430 --> 00:02:00,268
Pending means data was missing, so it waits.

20
00:02:00,741 --> 00:02:02,889
Your funnel shows up on the dashboard:

21
00:02:02,909 --> 00:02:05,914
as Dynamic funnel above the crypto and equity tables,

22
00:02:05,934 --> 00:02:08,060
and as a tile in Quick Snapshot.

23
00:02:08,110 --> 00:02:10,906
Turn on alerts to hear about new Candidates.
